# Firebase web configuration — copy to `.env` and fill from your own project.
#
#   Firebase console → Project settings → Your apps → SDK setup and configuration
#
# These values are PUBLIC identifiers, not secrets. The Firebase web SDK ships
# them in the client bundle by design; authorisation comes from Firestore
# security rules, not from keeping the key hidden. Anyone who reads `apiKey` in
# devtools learns which project the app points at — and nothing else.
#
# ⚠ A service-account key must NEVER appear here or in any `VITE_` var. It would
#   be baked into the client bundle and handed to every visitor, bypassing the
#   security rules entirely. Server-side tooling only, outside the client build.
#
# Never commit a real `.env`. This repository ships placeholders only, so forks
# never write to someone else's quota.

VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
